xt(r for r in reg['records'] if r['document_id']==b);y=next(r for r in m['documents'] if r['id']==a); print(a,'same bytes as P01',x['original_sha256']==y['sha256'])\\nprint('landing hash',hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_21\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,hashlib\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('data/financial-report-benchmark/landing/apple/21eae1adf76b91a72eab511c0a96cd56f2053878b8c22df5bfdbfdbb0adfcc42.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text());print('keys',list(d));r=d.get('filings',{}).get('recent',{})\\nfor i,f in enumerate(r.get('form',[])):\\n if f in ('10-K','10-Q','DEF 14A') and r['filingDate'][i]>='2024-10-01' and r['filingDate'][i]<='2025-02-01':\\n  print({k:v[i] for k,v in r.items() if k in ['form','filingDate','acceptanceDateTime','reportDate','accessionNumber','primaryDocument']})\\nm=json.loads(Path('docs/design/cases/apple/manifest.json').read_text());reg=json.loads(Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/source-work-register.json').read_text())\\nfor a,b in [('annual-2024.pdf','apple-2024-annual'),('interim-2025q1.html','apple-2025-q1')]:\\n x=next(r for r in reg['records'] if r['document_id']==b);y=next(r for r in m['documents'] if r['id']==a); print(a,'same bytes as P01',x['original_sha256']==y['sha256'])\\nprint('landing hash',hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"keys ['cik', 'entityType', 'sic', 'sicDescription', 'ownerOrg', 'insiderTransactionForOwnerExists', 'insiderTransactionForIssuerExists', 'name', 'tickers', 'exchanges', 'ein', 'lei', 'description', 'website', 'investorWebsite', 'category', 'fiscalYearEnd', 'stateOfIncorporation', 'stateOfIncorporationDescription', 'addresses', 'phone', 'flags', 'formerNames', 'filings']\\n{'accessionNumber': '0000320193-25-000008', 'filingDate': '2025-01-31', 'reportDate': '2024-12-28', 'acceptanceDateTime': '2025-01-31T16:01:27.000Z', 'form': '10-Q', 'primaryDocument': 'aapl-20241228.htm'}\\n{'accessionNumber': '0001308179-25-000008', 'filingDate': '2025-01-10', 'reportDate': '2025-02-25', 'acceptanceDateTime': '2025-01-11T02:31:18.000Z', 'form': 'DEF 14A', 'primaryDocument': 'aapl4359751-def14a.htm'}\\n{'accessionNumber': '0000320193-24-000123', 'filingDate': '2024-11-01', 'reportDate': '2024-09-28', 'acceptanceDateTime': '2024-11-01T14:01:36.000Z', 'form': '10-K', 'primaryDocument': 'aapl-20240928.htm'}\\nannual-2024.pdf same bytes as P01 True\\ninterim-2025q1.html same bytes as P01 True\\nlanding hash 21eae1adf76b91a72eab511c0a96cd56f2053878b8c22df5bfdbfdbb0adfcc42\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\" \"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_23\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The retained SEC index provides filing dates and accession IDs for both reports and the 2025 proxy. It does not establish the historical availability of the mirrored annual PDF. The annual cash-flow opening balance also includes restricted cash, so using balance-sheet cash alone would produce a wrong reconciliation.\\n\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '206,270p' docs/design/chapters/13-reference-company.tex; sed -n '1916,1933p' docs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt; sed -n '1732,1755p' docs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt; sed -n '995,1090p' docs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_24\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '206,270p' docs/design/chapters/13-reference-company.tex; sed -n '1916,1933p' docs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt; sed -n '1732,1755p' docs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt; sed -n '995,1090p' docs/design/cases/apple/interim-2025q1.txt\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\\\section{Apple: source labels do not identify exposure}\\n\\\\label{sec:apple}\\n\\nThe real reference package is Apple's 2024 Form 10-K and first-quarter 2025\\nForm 10-Q, for fiscal dates 28 September and 28 December 2024 respectively\\n\\\\citep{apple2024,apple2025q1}. The annual balance sheet also supplies\\n30 September 2023. The annual filing is archived as the company's PDF from\\nAnnualReports; the interim filing is archived from SEC EDGAR with its inline\\nXBRL. Apple's Note 1 describes a 52/53-week year ending on the last Saturday\\nof September. Calendar-year assumptions would therefore misstate the periods.\\n\\nThe package inventory preserves every annual PDF page and every interim\\ntop-level section, all thirteen annual notes and all ten interim notes.\\nIt records internal cross-references and externally incorporated material,\\nincluding the proxy statement, as distinct obligations. Statement and debt\\nfacts below are structured; policies, other notes and exhibits retain their\\nsource locations and specific modelling obligations. This is complete\\ninventory coverage of the acquired files, with partial semantic formalisation.\\nIt does not claim to reconstruct every Apple contract or to have acquired\\nevery incorporated external document.\\n\\nApple's annual balance sheet reports assets 364,980, liabilities 308,030 and\\nequity 56,950, in millions of US dollars. Note 9 reports term-debt principal\\n97,341, unamortised discount/premium and issuance costs of $-321$, and hedge\\naccounting adjustments of $-358$. Thus its carrying amount is\\n$97{,}341-321-358=96{,}662$, split into current 10,912 and non-current\\n85,750. Fair value is separately disclosed as 88.4 billion. None of these\\nthree measurements may replace another merely because a table calls it debt.\\n\\nNote 9 identifies the notes as fixed-rate, then states that interest-rate\\nswaps effectively convert a portion to floating rates. Note 4 reports\\ninterest-rate contract notional of 14,575 at the annual date. A notional is\\nneither a liability carrying amount nor sufficient information for an exact\\ninterest sensitivity: reset timing, remaining periods, curve conventions and\\nhedge coverage still matter. The cross-reference connects the derivative to\\nthe borrowing without erasing either contract.\\n\\nAt the interim date, total term-debt carrying amount is\\n$10{,}848+83{,}956=94{,}804$. Cash is 30,299, total assets 344,085,\\nliabilities 277,327 and equity 66,758. The interim debt note's rounded\\n``94.8 billion'' and the statement's 94,804 million can coexist; their\\nprecision differs. Treating them as conflicting exact numbers would create\\nan artificial infeasibility.\\n\\nTo demonstrate a source-to-forecast calculation, freeze the interim balance\\nsheet and apply a \\\\emph{marginal} financing stress for a following 13-week\\nperiod: a 200-basis-point rate increase, no principal change, no offsetting\\nhedge beyond the explicitly selected exposure, immediate cash settlement and\\nno tax effect. An assumed effective floating exposure $E=14{,}575$ million\\nproduces $0.02\\\\times(13/52)E=72.875$ million additional interest. This exposure\\nuses the annual notional as a conditional input; it is not asserted to be the\\ninterim net sensitivity. Under that condition, debit interest expense and\\ncredit cash by 72.875. The resulting marginal statements have cash 30,226.125,\\nassets 344,012.125, liabilities 277,327, equity 66,685.125, profit and comprehensive\\nincome of $-72.875$, and operating cash flow of $-72.875$ relative to the frozen\\nbaseline. The balance-sheet difference equals the equity difference exactly.\\n\\nIf exposure is instead only restricted to $0\\\\leq E\\\\leq14{,}575$, the\\nconditional added interest lies in $[0,72.875]$ before monetary rounding. That\\nrestriction is a stress assumption and is not claimed to bound every real\\nApple exposure. This real case verifies evidence, context, mappings and a\\ncoherent marginal propagation. Northstar supplies the complete-company\\nforecast; a complete Apple forecast remains dependent on its unmodelled\\noperations and undisclosed terms.\\n\\n\\n    (1)    The valuation techniques used to measure the fair values of the Company’s Level 2 financial instruments, which generally have counterparties with high credit\\n           ratings, are based on quoted market prices or model-driven valuations using significant inputs derived from or corroborated by observable market data.\\n    (2)    As of September 28, 2024, cash and cash equivalents included $2.6 billion held in escrow and restricted from general use. These restricted cash and cash\\n           equivalents were designated to settle the Company’s obligation related to the State Aid Decision (refer to Note 7, “Income Taxes”).\\n    (3)    As of September 28, 2024 and September 30, 2023, total marketable securities included $13.2 billion and $13.8 billion, respectively, held in escrow and\\n           restricted from general use. The September 28, 2024 restricted marketable securities were designated to settle the Company’s obligation related to the State Aid\\n           Decision (refer to Note 7, “Income Taxes”).\\n\\n\\nAs of September 28, 2024, 86% of the Company’s non-current marketable debt securities other than mortgage- and asset-backed securities had maturities\\nbetween 1 and 5 years, 10% between 5 and 10 years, and 4% greater than 10 years. As of September 28, 2024, 14% of the Company’s non-current mortgage-\\nand asset-backed securities had maturities between 1 and 5 years, 9% between 5 and 10 years, and 77% greater than 10 years.\\n\\nThe Company’s investments in marketable debt securities have been classified and accounted for as available-for-sale. The Company classifies marketable debt\\nsecurities as either current or non-current based on each instrument’s underlying maturity.\\n\\nNote 6 –\\nDebt\\nCommercial Paper\\nThe Company issues unsecured short-term promissory notes pursuant to a commercial paper program. The Company uses net proceeds from the commercial paper program for general corporate purposes, including dividends and share repurchases. As of December 28, 2024 and September 28, 2024, the Company had $\\n2.0\\nbillion and $\\n10.0\\nbillion of commercial paper outstanding, respectively.\\nTerm Debt\\nAs of December 28, 2024 and September 28, 2024, the Company had outstanding fixed-rate notes with varying maturities for an aggregate carrying amount of $\\n94.8\\nbillion\\nand $\\n96.7\\nbillion, respectively (collectively the “Notes”). As of December 28, 2024 and September 28, 2024, the fair value of the Company’s Notes, based on Level 2 inputs, was\\n$\\n82.7\\nbillion and $\\n88.4\\nbillion, respectively.\\nNote 7 –\\nShareholders’ Equity\\nShare Repurchase Program\\nDuring the three months ended December 28, 2024, the Company repurchased\\nDecember 30,\\n2023\\nCash, cash equivalents, and restricted cash and cash equivalents, beginning balances\\n$\\n29,943\\n$\\n30,737\\nOperating activities:\\nNet income\\n36,330\\n33,916\\nAdjustments to reconcile net income to cash generated by operating activities:\\nDepreciation and amortization\\n3,080\\n2,848\\nShare-based compensation expense\\n3,286\\n2,997\\nOther\\n(\\n2,009\\n)\\n(\\n989\\n)\\nChanges in operating assets and liabilities:\\nAccounts receivable, net\\n3,597\\n6,555\\nVendor non-trade receivables\\n3,166\\n4,569\\nInventories\\n215\\n(\\n137\\n)\\nOther current and non-current assets\\n939\\n(\\n1,457\\n)\\nAccounts payable\\n(\\n6,671\\n)\\n(\\n4,542\\n)\\nOther current and non-current liabilities\\n(\\n11,998\\n)\\n(\\n3,865\\n)\\nCash generated by operating activities\\n29,935\\n39,895\\nInvesting activities:\\nPurchases of marketable securities\\n(\\n6,124\\n)\\n(\\n9,780\\n)\\nProceeds from maturities of marketable securities\\n15,967\\n13,046\\nProceeds from sales of marketable securities\\n3,492\\n1,337\\nPayments for acquisition of property, plant and equipment\\n(\\n2,940\\n)\\n(\\n2,392\\n)\\nOther\\n(\\n603\\n)\\n(\\n284\\n)\\nCash generated by investing activities\\n9,792\\n1,927\\nFinancing activities:\\nPayments for taxes related to net share settlement of equity awards\\n(\\n2,921\\n)\\n(\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_25\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,re\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nm=json.loads(Path('docs/design/cases/apple/manifest.json').read_text())\\nfor doc in ['annual','interim']:\\n t=Path('docs/design/cases/apple/'+('annual-2024.txt' if doc=='annual' else 'interim-2025q1.txt')).read_text()\\n print(doc,'independent headings',len(list(re.finditer(r'(?m)\\\"'^['\\\"\\\\\\\\f \\\\\\\\t]*Note (\\\\\\\\d+)\\\\\\\\s*[–-]\\\\\\\\s*([\\\"'^'\\\"\\\\\\\\n]+)',t))))\\n for n in m['notes']:\\n  if n['source']==doc and not re.match(r'\\\"'^['\\\"\\\\\\\\f \\\\\\\\t]*Note '+str(n['number'])+r'\\\\\\\\s*[–-]',t[n['start_character']:n['end_character']]): print('bad',n['id'])\\np=Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/checks.json'); print('P01 checks',p.read_text()[:1800])\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_25\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"python3 -B - <<'PY'\\nimport json,re\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nm=json.loads(Path('docs/design/cases/apple/manifest.json').read_text())\\nfor doc in ['annual','interim']:\\n t=Path('docs/design/cases/apple/'+('annual-2024.txt' if doc=='annual' else 'interim-2025q1.txt')).read_text()\\n print(doc,'independent headings',len(list(re.finditer(r'(?m)\\\"'^['\\\"\\\\\\\\f \\\\\\\\t]*Note (\\\\\\\\d+)\\\\\\\\s*[–-]\\\\\\\\s*([\\\"'^'\\\"\\\\\\\\n]+)',t))))\\n for n in m['notes']:\\n  if n['source']==doc and not re.match(r'\\\"'^['\\\"\\\\\\\\f \\\\\\\\t]*Note '+str(n['number'])+r'\\\\\\\\s*[–-]',t[n['start_character']:n['end_character']]): print('bad',n['id'])\\np=Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T180732-83972f09/P01/checks.json'); print('P01 checks',p.read_text()[:1800])\\nPY\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"annual independent headings 13\\ninterim independent headings 10\\nP01 checks {\\n  \\\"passed\\\": true,\\n  \\\"tests\\\": 580,\\n  \\\"checks\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"explicit bounded acceptance\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"deliverable source-work-register.json\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"exact source IDs\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"register input hashes\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-annual source binding\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-annual source context\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-annual no semantic promotion\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q1 source binding\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q1 source context\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q1 no semantic promotion\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q2 source binding\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q2 source context\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q2 no semantic promotion\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q3 source binding\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q3 source context\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2018-q3 no semantic promotion\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2019-annual source binding\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2019-annual source context\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2019-annual no semantic promotion\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2019-q1 source binding\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"apple-2019-q1 source context\\\",\\n      \\\"passed\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"a\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_26\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\" \"}}\n\n--- prompt ---\nYou are a sequential worker for the user-authorised AccDSL master program.\nRole: plan. Repository: /home/chakwong/python/AccDSL. Phase contract follows below.\nWork from this current phase packet and relevant code/source evidence. The master plan preserves MC01–MC35 and G1–G18. Consult specific requirement rows when needed; do not repeat whole-project or historical gap audits.\nNo agents/delegation/recursive workers. Do not launch another model or this master runner. Do not start detached/background jobs.\nNo paid service/data, accounts, outreach, publication, deployment, global or conda package installation, Git initialization, source deletion or permission changes.\nNever use approval/sandbox bypass. Do not request approvals. Record inaccessible capabilities once and continue independent authorised work.\nOnly implement/repair roles may edit project code and the phase deliverables. Planner/reviewer roles are strictly read-only.\nDo not edit the master controller, support module, catalog, response schema, controller tests or master plan. Under data/accounting-master you may write only your declared deliverables; all other supervisor files are protected from worker edits.\nDo not modify data/financial-report-benchmark or any file pinned by its release manifest. Do not modify preserved pre-repair/pre-expert snapshots.\nPreserve unrelated work. Add new versioned modules/results instead of rewriting frozen evidence. Record all changed source/code/test files in evidence.\nUse only standard-library/existing packages by default. Any essential new open-source dependency must be isolated under this project, version-pinned and documented.\nPublic-source research must use legitimate official/primary sources, preserve local copies and exact support; no challenge bypass or fabricated authority.\nSeparate specified behaviour, implemented code, tested invariants, accounting validity, empirical forecast validity and human acceptance. All G1–G18 retain their wider obligations.\nBefore scientific runs, write the research intent/evidence/default audit and matched baseline plan required by project policy. Short checks cannot establish superiority.\nFor PLAN, inspect existing artifacts and produce concrete implementation steps, explicit assumptions, exact checks, risks/nonclaims and residuals. Address every supplied review finding before revising a plan.\nFor review_plan, actively check wrong baselines, proxy promotion, missing stops, unfair comparisons, hidden assumptions, stale context, environment mismatch and whether proposed artifacts answer the question. AGREE requires no unresolved material objection.\nFor implement/repair, execute the reviewed plan, write the specified actual deliverables and meaningful unittest cases at the required test_file. Execute checks and fix failures. Do not merely write a plan or call authored expected values the implementation.\nFor review_result, inspect actual code, tests, source evidence and deterministic check reports. A returned success or many tests alone is insufficient. Return REVISE with actionable repairs if acceptance criteria fail.\nAn AGREE response must have issues=[]; put nonblocking limitations in residuals. An empty implementation or a plan-only deliverable must not pass an implementation phase.\nFor review_controller, audit orchestration, recovery, permissions, repair, plan refresh, child-process limits and honest completion against the plan and tests. Do not change files.\nEvery evidence entry must be an existing repository-relative FILE path, never prose, a directory or an invented artifact. Include concrete unresolved work in residuals and justified next tasks in next_actions.\nReturn only the response schema. Verdict: PLAN for plan; AGREE/REVISE for review; IMPLEMENTED for actual work; BLOCKED only for a real dependency preventing the stated slice. Explain partial work without claiming whole-gap closure.\nReturn a JSON object with ALL these exact keys and array/string types (fill with actual findings; no extra keys): {\"verdict\": \"PLAN\", \"summary\": \"Replace with the actual finding\", \"steps\": [], \"assumptions\": [], \"checks\": [], \"evidence\": [], \"issues\": [], \"residuals\": [], \"next_actions\": []}\n{\n  \"phase\": {\n    \"id\": \"P02\",\n    \"kind\": \"worker\",\n    \"name\": \"Complete the bounded Apple case preparation\",\n    \"deps\": [\n      \"P01\"\n    ],\n    \"gaps\": [\n      \"G4\",\n      \"G5\",\n      \"G11\",\n      \"G12\",\n      \"G13\"\n    ],\n    \"requirements\": [\n      \"MC01\",\n      \"MC03\",\n      \"MC05\",\n      \"MC16\",\n      \"MC28\"\n    ],\n    \"objective\": \"Build a source-anchored annual/interim Apple case layer over the existing retained files: every inventoried note has an explicit modelling disposition, selected statement/note bridges are machine-checked, external incorporations remain visible, and known unidentified histories are preserved. I