{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'MC01|MC03|MC05|MC16|MC28|G4|G5|G11|G12|G13' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md docs/plans/accounting-master-program.md docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:124:### G4. The first corporate accounting package is an inventory of duties\ndocs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:145:### G5. No complete filing-to-forecast reference case tests the central workflow\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:36:to the [initial gap audit](../design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md); G11–G18 refer\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:55:| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:56:| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:57:| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:59:| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:60:| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:61:| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:77:| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:79:| MC15 | Specify ordinary corporate operations and accounting across periods. U1, U2, U3, D. | Provide a bounded coherent package for revenue/collections, purchases/payments, inventory/costs, assets/depreciation, payroll, financing and applicable closing/tax assumptions, with explicit exclusions. | Specified bounded corporate package in Chs. 2, 8 with exact annual/interim and forecast fixtures. Delivery, collection, purchase, payment, costs, plant, payroll, debt, simple tax and closing reconcile. Real tax/revenue/lease/FX packages remain separate work. G4, G5. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:80:| MC16 | Produce coherent financial statements, movements and supported note schedules from the same underlying history/path. U1, U2, D. | Define balance sheet, income/comprehensive income, cash flow and equity mappings, non-cash movements, closing and note relationships; supply a full set of expected outputs. | Reference-checked complete Northstar balance sheet, income/zero OCI, direct/indirect cash flow and equity from common journals; Chs. 2, 8 and `northstar.json`. Apple checks a coherent marginal financing stress only. General note schedules and report engine remain pending. G4, G5, G6. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:81:| MC17 | Represent financing instruments and their economic/accounting lifecycles, particularly bonds and equity. U1, U2, D. | Specify proceeds, principal, carrying/fair values, rates, calendars, maturities, rights and share quantities; work issuance, accrual, settlement and relevant modification/conversion/default cases under declared treatments. | Partially specified and reference-checked: Chs. 8–9 distinguish principal/carrying/fair values and work ordinary and convertible bond issue, accrual, redemption/conversion, shares and funding default. Detailed modification, early repurchase and other-basis hybrid classification remain open. G4, G7. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:88:| MC19 | Accommodate IFRS, US GAAP and China GAAP/ASBE with dated treatments, elections and transitions. U1, U3. | Define the supported treatment matrix, rule authority and version selection; show matched economic events under selected genuinely different treatments and identify unimplemented operations. | Partially repaired. Ch. 9 compares FIFO/LIFO/average and records dated rule selection. Selected IAS-equivalent paragraphs inspected in official AASB texts; US LIFO has company-policy evidence only, full ASC authority is blocked, and official ASBE version verification remains pending. Source dossiers record exact edition/period limits and correct Caterpillar inventories to Note 8. G7, G8, G13. The acquired panel now supplies report-level preparation-basis evidence across US GAAP, IFRS-oriented reporting and ASBE; this does not replace dated primary accounting authority. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:89:| MC20 | Support materially different industry and company concepts without bypassing the common accounting semantics. U1, D. | Specify extension points, concept mappings and rule admissibility; include representative industry differences and an invalid company override. | Specified extension points, override admission, separate books and mappings in Chs. 3, 7, 9/Core 0. Inventory/bank/insurer structures expose distinct state requirements. Full invalid-override and package-conformance execution remains pending. G2, G7, G12. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:98:| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:102:| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G5, G7. Nine eight-year report sequences are now source-checked; report-wide semantic cases and executable oracles remain to be prepared. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:116:| MC32 | Deliver a detailed, readable LaTeX/PDF document that governs the intended implementation. U3, P. | Explain the whole problem, justify chosen methods, stage mathematical prerequisites, define supported behaviour and disclose open scope; connect derivations and sources to complete examples and interfaces. Preserve mathematical/source fidelity during revisions and inspect the rendered result. | Revised Version 1.2 candidate, 11 chapters plus two appendices, full cases and supporting normative files. Build, rendered inspection and baseline-preservation review are recorded in `review/author-review.md`. Human comprehension, domain review and independent implementability acceptance remain pending. G1, G2, G4, G5, G7, G10. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:122:| MC33 | Define meaningful acceptance and separate engineering, accounting and scientific evidence. U3, P, D. | Provide canonical conformance inputs/outputs, corpus/annotation rules, justified release-specific criteria, review status and later forecast baselines/uncertainty protocols. Existing arithmetic/build checks keep their limited meanings. | Specified fixtures, corpus strata, annotation/adjudication/split protocol, hard conformance vetoes and provisional workload limits in Ch. 11/`corpus-protocol.json`. Reference checks, new debt semantic rejection cases, accounting dossiers and author review recorded; the 192-report source panel now passes acquisition acceptance and independent integrity checks. Annotation protocol/schema and provisional family roles exist; adjudication, performance and release validation remain pending. G5, G10. |\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:140:plan; v1 evidence remains preserved. This advances MC01, MC03, MC05, MC19–22,\ndocs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md:141:MC28, MC30 and MC33–35 without closing semantic, accounting or forecast\ndocs/plans/accounting-master-program.md:3:Date: 2 October 2026. User authority: create, review and execute a master program for the consolidated gaps, with actual repair, refreshed plans between phases, and reusable upfront approvals. Scope: MC01–MC35 and G1–G18; the existing mission remains authoritative.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:5:[MC01–MC34 requirements](../../plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:39:### G11. Whole-report coverage and narrative formalisation need a procedure\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:41:Requirements: MC01, MC03. Refines G2 and G5.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:60:### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:62:Requirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:79:### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:81:Requirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\ndocs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md:158:Requirements: MC04, MC27. Refines G2, G5 and G10.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
