{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"reasoning","text":"**Exploring rounding strategies**\n\nI’m considering exact rounding intervals and how they should function, possibly between conservative closed and half-open criteria. I don’t want any fabricated tie rules. The default would be rounding to the nearest, keeping half-unit closed with conservative intervals, ensuring the boundary policies are inclusive. For accurate financial records, I'll display point identities without inferring underlying values. I need to ensure tolerances are specified rather than arbitrary, using Minkowski sums for interval handling."}}
