ual-2024.txt-2823-                   4.100% Notes due 2062.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2824-\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3068-                                                                                   2\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3069-\f                                                              DESCRIPTION OF DEBT SECURITIES\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3070-         The following description of the Notes is a summary and does not purport to be complete. This description is qualified in its entirety by reference, as\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3071:applicable, to the Indenture, dated as of April 29, 2013, between Apple Inc. and The Bank of New York Mellon Trust Company, N.A., as trustee (the “2013\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3072:Indenture”) and the Indenture, dated as of November 5, 2018, between Apple Inc. and The Bank of New York Mellon Trust Company, N.A., as trustee (the “2018\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3073:Indenture,” and together with the 2013 Indenture, the “Indentures”). References in this section to the “Company,” “us,” “we” and “our” are solely to Apple Inc. and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3074-not to any of its subsidiaries, unless the context requires otherwise.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3075-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3076-The Notes\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3077:          Each of the Notes were issued under the applicable Indenture, which provides that debt securities may be issued under such Indenture from time to\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3078:time in one or more series. The Indentures and the Notes are governed by, and construed in accordance with, the laws of the State of New York. The Indentures\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3079-do not limit the amount of debt securities that we may issue thereunder. We may, without the consent of the holders of the debt securities of any series, issue\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3080-additional debt securities ranking equally with, and otherwise similar in all respects to, the debt securities of the series (except for the date of issuance, the date\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3081-interest begins to accrue and, in certain circumstances, the first interest payment date) so that those additional debt securities will be consolidated and form a\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3082-single series with the debt securities of the series previously offered and sold; provided, however, that any additional debt securities will have a separate ISIN\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3083-number unless certain conditions are met.\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3131-indebtedness from time to time outstanding. However, the Notes are structurally subordinated to any indebtedness and preferred stock, if any, of our subsidiaries\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3132-and are effectively subordinated to any secured indebtedness to the extent of the value of the assets securing such indebtedness. Claims of the creditors of our\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3133-subsidiaries generally have priority with respect to the assets and earnings of such subsidiaries over the claims of our creditors, including holders of the Notes.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3134:Accordingly, the Notes are effectively subordinated to creditors, including trade creditors and preferred stockholders, if any, of our subsidiaries. The Indentures\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3135-do not restrict our ability or that of our subsidiaries to incur additional indebtedness.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3136-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3137-Payment on the Notes\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3138-          All payments of principal of, the redemption price (if any), and interest and additional amounts (if any) on the 0.000% 2025 Notes, the 0.875% 2025\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3139-Notes, the 2026 Notes, the 2027 Notes, the 1.375% 2029 Notes and the 2031 Notes are payable in euro, provided that, if the euro is unavailable to the\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3145-Day prior to the relevant payment date or, in the event the U.S. Federal Reserve Board has not mandated a rate of conversion, on the basis of the most recent\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3146-U.S. dollar/euro exchange rate published in The Wall Street Journal on or prior to the second Business Day prior to the relevant payment date. Any payment in\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3147-respect of the 0.000% 2025 Notes, the 0.875% 2025 Notes, the 2026 Notes, the 2027 Notes, the 1.375% 2029 Notes and the 2031 Notes so made in U.S.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3148:dollars will not constitute an event of default under such Notes or the applicable Indenture.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3149-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3150-         With respect to the 0.000% 2025 Notes, the 0.875% 2025 Notes, the 2026 Notes, the 2027 Notes, the 1.375% 2029 Notes and the 2031 Notes,\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3151-“Business Day” means any day, other than a Saturday or Sunday, (1) which is not a day on which banking institutions in The City of New York or London are\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3152-authorized or required by law, regulation or executive order to close and (2) on which the Trans-European Automated Real-time Gross Settlement Express\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3153-Transfer system (the TARGET2 system), or any successor thereto, is open.\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3167-second Business Day prior to the relevant payment date or, in the event the U.S. Federal Reserve Board has not mandated a rate of conversion, on the basis of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3168-the most recent U.S. dollar/pounds sterling or, in the event the Notes are redenominated into euro, the most recent U.S. dollar/euro exchange rate published in\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3169-The Wall Street Journal on or prior to the second Business Day prior to the relevant payment date. Any payment in respect of the 3.050% 2029 Notes and the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3170:2042 Notes so made in U.S. dollars will not constitute an event of default under such Notes or the 2013 Indenture.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3171-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3172-        With respect to the 3.050% 2029 Notes and the 2042 Notes, “Business Day” means any day which is not a day on which banking institutions in The City\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3173-of New York or London or the relevant place of payment are authorized or required by law, regulation or executive order to close.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3174-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3175-Payment of Additional Amounts\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3304-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3305-         Installments of interest on Notes being redeemed that are due and payable on interest payment dates falling on or prior to a redemption date shall be\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3306-payable on the interest payment date to the holders as of the close of business on the relevant regular record date according to the Notes and the applicable\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3307:Indenture.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3308-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3309-         “Comparable Government Bond” means, in relation to any Comparable Government Bond Rate calculation for the 2026 Notes and the 2027 Notes, at\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3310-the discretion of an independent investment bank selected by us, a German government bond whose maturity is closest to the maturity of the Notes being\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3311-redeemed, or if such independent investment bank in its discretion determines that such similar bond is not in issue, such other German government bond as\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3312-such independent investment bank may, with the advice of three brokers of, and/or market\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3336-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3337-Covenants\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3338-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3339:         The Indentures set forth limited covenants that apply to the Notes. However, these covenants do not, among other things:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3340-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3341-         •   limit the amount of indebtedness or lease obligations that may be incurred by us and our subsidiaries;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3342-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3343-         •   limit our ability or that of our subsidiaries to issue, assume or guarantee debt secured by liens; or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3344-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3345-         •   restrict us from paying dividends or making distributions on our capital stock or purchasing or redeeming our capital stock.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3346-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3347-         Consolidation, Merger and Sale of Assets\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3348:         The Indentures provide that we may consolidate with or merge with or into any other person, and may sell, transfer, or lease or convey all or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3349-substantially all of our properties and assets to another person; provided that the following conditions are satisfied:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3350-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3351-         •   we are the continuing entity, or the resulting, surviving or transferee person (the “Successor”) is a person (if such person is not a corporation, then\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3352-             the Successor will include a corporate co-issuer of the debt securities) organized and existing under the laws of the United States of America, any\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3353-             state thereof or the District of Columbia and the Successor (if not us) will expressly assume, by supplemental indenture, all of our obligations under\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3354:             the debt securities and the applicable Indenture and, for each security that by its terms provides for conversion, provide for the right to convert such\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3355-             security in accordance with its terms;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3356-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3357:         •   immediately after giving effect to such transaction, no default or event of default under the applicable Indenture has occurred and is continuing; and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3358-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3359:         •   in the case of the 2013 Indenture, the trustee receives from us an officers’ certificate and an opinion of counsel that the transaction and such\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3360:             supplemental indenture, as the case may be, complies with the applicable provisions of the 2013 Indenture.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3361-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3362-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3363-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3364-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3365-                                                                                  8\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3366-\f         If we consolidate or merge with or into any other person or sell, transfer, lease or convey all or substantially all of our properties and assets in\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3367:accordance with the Indentures, the Successor will be substituted for us in the Indentures, with the same effect as if it had been an original party to the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3368:Indentures. As a result, the Successor may exercise our rights and powers under the Indentures, and we will be released from all our liabilities and obligations\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3369:under the Indentures and under the debt securities.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3370-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3371-       For purposes of this covenant, “person” means any individual, corporation, partnership, limited liability company, joint venture, association, joint-stock\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3372-company, trust, unincorporated organization or government or any agency or political subdivision thereof or any other entity.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3373-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3374-Events of Default\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3375:          Each of the following events are defined in the Indentures as an “event of default” (whatever the reason for such event of default and whether or not it\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3376-will be voluntary or involuntary or be effected by operation of law or pursuant to any judgment, decree or order of any court or any order, rule or regulation of any\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3377-administrative or governmental body) with respect to the debt securities of any series:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3378-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3379-         (1)   default in the payment of any installment of interest on any debt securities of such series for 30 days after becoming due;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3380-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3381-         (2)   default in the payment of principal of or premium, if any, on any debt securities of such series when it becomes due and payable at its stated\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3382-               maturity, upon optional redemption, upon declaration or otherwise;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3383-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3384:         (3)    default in the performance, or breach, of any covenant or agreement of ours in the applicable Indenture with respect to the debt securities of such\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3385:               series (other than a covenant or agreement, a default in the performance of which or a breach of which is elsewhere in the applicable Indenture\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3386:               specifically dealt with or that has expressly been included in the applicable Indenture solely for the benefit of a series of debt securities other than\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3387-               such series), which continues for a period of 90 days after written notice to us by the trustee or to us and the trustee by the holders of, in the case\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3388:               of the 2013 Indenture, at least 25% in aggregate principal amount of the outstanding debt securities of that series, and in the case of the 2018\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3389:               Indenture, at least 33% in aggregate principal amount of the outstanding debt securities of that series;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3390-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3391-         (4)   we, pursuant to or within the meaning of the Bankruptcy Law:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3392-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3393-               •   commence a voluntary case or proceeding;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3394-\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3412-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3413-               •   orders the winding-up or liquidation of us (or any similar relief is granted under any foreign laws);\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3414-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3415:               and the order or decree remains unstayed and in effect for 90 days (or, in the case of the 2018 Indenture, 90 consecutive days); or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3416-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3417-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3418-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3419-                                                                                     9\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3420-\f         (6)   any other event of default provided with respect to debt securities of such series occurs.\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3423-custodian, receiver, trustee, assignee, liquidator or other similar official under any Bankruptcy Law.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3424-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3425-         If an event of default with respect to debt securities of any series (other than an event of default relating to certain events of bankruptcy, insolvency, or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3426:reorganization of us) occurs and is continuing, the trustee by notice to us, or the holders of, in the case of the 2013 Indenture, at least 25% in aggregate principal\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3427:amount of the outstanding debt securities of such series, and in the case of the 2018 Indenture, at least 33% in aggregate principal amount of the outstanding\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3428-debt securities of such series, by notice to us and the trustee, may, and the trustee at the request of these holders will, declare the principal of and premium, if\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3429-any, and accrued and unpaid interest on all the debt securities of such series to be due and payable. Upon such a declaration, such principal, premium and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3430-accrued and unpaid interest will be due and payable immediately. If an event of default relating to certain events of bankruptcy, insolvency, or reorganization of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3431-us occurs and is continuing, the principal of and premium, if any, and accrued and unpaid interest on the debt securities of such series will become and be\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3432-immediately due and payable without any declaration or other act on the part of the trustee or any holders.\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3434-         The holders of not less than a majority in aggregate principal amount of the outstanding debt securities of any series may rescind a declaration of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3435-acceleration and its consequences, if we have deposited certain sums with the trustee and all events of default with respect to the debt securities of such series,\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3436-other than the non-payment of the principal or interest which have become due solely by such acceleration, have been cured or waived, as provided in the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3437:Indentures.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3438-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3439-        An event of default for a particular series of debt securities does not necessarily constitute an event of default for any other series of debt securities\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3440:issued under the Indentures.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3441-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3442-          We are required to furnish the trustee annually within 120 days after the end of our fiscal year a statement by one of our officers to the effect that, to the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3443:best knowledge of such officer, we are not in default in the fulfillment of any of our obligations under the applicable Indenture or, if there has been a default in the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3444-fulfillment of any such obligation, specifying each such default and the nature and status thereof.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3445-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3446:          No holder of any debt securities of any series will have any right to institute any judicial or other proceeding with respect to the applicable Indenture, or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3447-for the appointment of a receiver or trustee, or for any other remedy unless:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3448-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3449-         (1)   an event of default has occurred and is continuing and such holder has given the trustee prior written notice of such continuing event of default\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3450-               with respect to the debt securities of such series;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3451-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3452:         (2)    in the case of the 2013 Indenture, the holders of not less than 25% of the aggregate principal amount of the outstanding debt securities of such\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3453:               series, and in the case of the 2018 Indenture, the holders of not less than 33% of the aggregate principal amount of the outstanding debt securities\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3454-               of such series have requested the trustee to institute proceedings in respect of such event of default;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3455-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3456-         (3)   the trustee has been offered indemnity reasonably satisfactory to it against its costs, expenses and liabilities in complying with such request;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3457-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3458-         (4)   the trustee has failed to institute proceedings 60 days after the receipt of such notice, request and offer of indemnity; and\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3462-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3463-          The holders of a majority in aggregate principal amount of outstanding debt securities of a series will have the right, subject to certain limitations, to\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3464-direct the time, method and place of conducting any proceeding for any remedy available to the trustee with respect to the debt securities of that series or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3465:exercising any trust or power conferred to the trustee, and to waive certain defaults. Each of the Indentures provides that if an event of default occurs and is\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3466:continuing, the trustee will exercise such of its rights and powers under such Indenture, and use the same degree of care and skill in their exercise, as a prudent\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3467-person would exercise or use under the circumstances in\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3468-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3469-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3470-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3471-                                                                                   10\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3472-\fthe conduct of such person’s own affairs. Subject to such provisions, the trustee will be under no obligation to exercise any of its rights or powers under the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3473:applicable Indenture at the request of any of the holders of the debt securities of a series unless they will have offered to the trustee security or indemnity\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3474-satisfactory to the trustee against the costs, expenses and liabilities which might be incurred by it in compliance with such request.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3475-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3476-       Notwithstanding the foregoing, the holder of any debt security will have an absolute and unconditional right to receive payment of the principal of and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3477-premium, if any, and interest on that debt security on or after the due dates expressed in that debt security and to institute suit for the enforcement of payment.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3478-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3479-Modification and Waivers\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3480:          Modification and amendments of the Indentures and the Notes may be made by us and the trustee with the consent of the holders of not less than a\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3481-majority in aggregate principal amount of the outstanding series of Notes affected thereby; provided, however, that no such modification or amendment may,\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3482-without the consent of the holder of each outstanding Note of that series affected thereby:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3483-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3484-         •   change the stated maturity of the principal of, or installment of interest on, any Note;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3485-\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3487-             acceleration of the maturity thereof or reduce the rate of interest on any Note;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3488-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3489-         •   reduce any premium payable on the redemption of any Note or change the date on which any Note may or must be redeemed (in the case of the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3490:             2018 Indenture, it being understood that a change to any notice requirement with respect to such date shall not be deemed to be a change of such\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3491-             date);\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3492-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3493-         •   change the coin or currency in which the principal of, premium, if any, or interest on any Note is payable;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3494-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3495-         •   impair the right of any holder to institute suit for the enforcement of any payment on or after the stated maturity of any Note (or, in the case of\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3497-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3498-         •   reduce the percentage in principal amount of the outstanding Notes, the consent of whose holders is required in order to take certain actions;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3499-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3500:         •   reduce the requirements for quorum or voting by holders of Notes in the applicable Indenture or the Note;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3501-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3502:         •   modify any of the provisions in the applicable Indenture regarding the waiver of past defaults and the waiver of certain covenants by the holders of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3503:             Notes except to increase any percentage vote required or to provide that certain other provisions of the applicable Indenture cannot be modified or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3504-             waived without the consent of the holder of each Notes affected thereby;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3505-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3506-         •   make any change that adversely affects the right to convert or exchange any debt security or decreases the conversion or exchange rate or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3507-             increases the conversion price of any convertible or exchangeable debt security, unless such decrease or increase is permitted by the terms of the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3508-             debt securities; or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3509-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3510-         •   modify any of the above provisions.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3511-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3512:         We and the trustee may, without the consent of any holders, modify or amend the terms of the Indentures and any series of Notes with respect to the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3513-following:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3514-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3515-         •   to add to our covenants for the benefit of holders of all or any series of the Notes or to surrender any right or power conferred upon us;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3516-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3517-         •   to evidence the succession of another person to, and the assumption by the successor of our covenants, agreements and obligations under, the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3518:             applicable Indenture pursuant to the covenant described above under the caption “Covenants—Consolidation, Merger and Sale of Assets”;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3519-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3520-         •   to add any additional events of default for the benefit of holders of all or any series of the Notes;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3521-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3522-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3523-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3524-                                                                                  11\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3525:\f         •    to add one or more guarantees, and in the case of the 2018 Indenture, co-obligors, for the benefit of holders of the Notes;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3526-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3527:         •    to secure the Notes pursuant to the covenants of the Indenture;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3528-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3529-         •    to add or appoint a successor or separate trustee or other agent;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3530-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3531-         •    to provide for the issuance of additional debt securities of any series;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3532-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3533:         •    to establish the form or terms of the debt securities of any series as permitted by the Indenture;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3534-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3535-         •    to comply with the rules of any applicable securities depository;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3536-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3537-         •    to provide for uncertificated Notes in addition to or in place of certificated Notes;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3538-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3539:         •    in the case of the 2013 Indenture, to add to, change or eliminate any of the provisions of the 2013 Indenture in respect of one or more series of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3540-              debt securities; provided that any such addition, change or elimination (a) shall neither (1) apply to any debt security of any series created prior to\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3541-              the execution of such supplemental indenture and entitled to the benefit of such provision nor (2) modify the rights of the holder of any such debt\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3542-              security with respect to such provision or (b) shall become effective only when there is no debt security described in clause (a)(1) outstanding;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3543-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3544:         •    in the case of the 2018 Indenture, to add to, change or eliminate any of the provisions of the 2018 Indenture in respect of one or more series of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3545-              debt securities; provided that any such addition, change or elimination shall become effective only when there is no outstanding security of any\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3546-              series created prior to the execution of such supplemental indenture that is entitled to the benefit of such provision and as to which such\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3547-              supplemental indenture would apply;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3548-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3549-         •    to cure any ambiguity, omission, defect or inconsistency;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3550-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3551-         •    to change any other provision; provided that the change does not adversely affect the interests of the holders of debt securities of, in the case of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3552:              the 2013 Indenture any series, and in the case of the 2018 Indenture, any outstanding series, in any material respect;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3553-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3554:         •    to supplement any of the provisions of the applicable Indenture to such extent as shall be necessary to permit or facilitate the defeasance and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3555:              discharge of any series of Notes pursuant to the Indenture; provided that any such action shall not adversely affect the interests of the holders of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3556-              Notes of such series or any other series of debt securities in any material respect;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3557-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3558-         •    to comply with the rules or regulations of any securities exchange or automated quotation system on which any of the Notes may be listed or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3559-              traded; and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3560-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3561:         •    to add to, change or eliminate any of the provisions of the applicable Indenture as shall be necessary or desirable in accordance with any\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3562:              amendments to the Trust Indenture Act of 1939, as amended, and in the case of the 2013 Indenture, provided that such action does not adversely\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3563-              affect the rights or interests of any holder of debt securities in any material respect.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3564-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3565-         The holders of at least a majority in aggregate principal amount of the outstanding Notes of any series may, on behalf of the holders of all Notes of that\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3566:series, waive compliance by us with certain restrictive provisions of the Indentures. The holders of not less than a majority in aggregate principal amount of the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3567-outstanding Notes of a series may, on behalf of the holders of all Notes of that series, waive any past default and its consequences under the applicable\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3568:Indenture with respect to the Notes of that series, except a default (1) in the payment of principal or premium, if any, or interest on Notes of that series or (2) in\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3569:respect of a covenant or provision of the applicable Indenture that cannot be modified or amended without the consent of the holder of each Note of that series.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3570-Upon any such waiver, such default will cease to exist, and any event of default arising therefrom will be deemed to have been cured, for every purpose of the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3571:Indenture; however, no such waiver will extend to any subsequent or other default or event of default or impair any rights consequent thereon.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3572-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3573-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3574-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3575-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3576-                                                                                    12\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3582-direct the trustee to invest such funds in U.S. Treasury securities with a maturity of one year or less or in a money market fund that invests solely in short-term\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3583-U.S. Treasury securities.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3584-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3585:          The Indentures provide that we may elect either (1) to defease and be discharged from any and all obligations with respect to the Notes of a series\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3586-(except for, among other things, obligations to register the transfer or exchange of the Notes, to replace temporary or mutilated, destroyed, lost or stolen Notes,\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3587-to maintain an office or agency with respect to the Notes and to hold moneys for payment in trust) (“legal defeasance”) or (2) to be released from our obligations\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3588:to comply with the restrictive covenants under the applicable Indenture, and any omission to comply with such obligations will not constitute a default or an event\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3589-of default with respect to the Notes of a series and clauses (3) and (6) under the caption “Events of Default” above will no longer be applied (“covenant\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3590-defeasance”). Legal defeasance or covenant defeasance, as the case may be, will be conditioned upon, among other things, the irrevocable deposit by us with\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3591-the trustee, in trust, of an amount in U.S. dollars, or U.S. government obligations (as such term is modified below), or both, applicable to the Notes of that series\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3592-which through the scheduled payment of principal and interest in accordance with their terms will provide money in an amount sufficient to pay the principal or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3593-premium, if any, and interest on the Notes on the scheduled due dates therefor.\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3633-integral multiples of £1,000 in excess thereof in the case of the 3.050% 2029 Notes and the 2042 Notes, if:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3634-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3635-         1.   the common depositary notifies us that it is unwilling or unable to continue as depositary or if the common depositary ceases to be eligible under\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3636:              the applicable Indenture and we do not appoint a successor depository within 90 days;\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3637-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3638-         2.   we determine that the Notes will no longer be represented by global securities and execute and deliver to the trustee an order to that effect; or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3639-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3640-         3.   an event of default with respect to the Notes will have occurred and be continuing.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3641-\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3644-be registered in the name of the common depositary or its nominee.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3645-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3646-The Trustee for the Notes\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:3647:          The Bank of New York Mellon Trust Company, N.A. is the trustee under the Indentures. We have commercial deposits and custodial arrangements with\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3648-The Bank of New York Mellon Trust Company, N.A. and its affiliates (“BNYM”). We may enter into similar or other banking relationships with BNYM in the future\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3649-in the normal course of business. In addition, BNYM acts as trustee and as paying agent with respect to other debt securities issued by us, and may do so for\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3650-future issuances of debt securities by us as well.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3651-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-3652-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"verdict\": \"PLAN\",\n  \"summary\": \"P02 can proceed as a bounded source-to-case implementation. Current retained-file hashes match the Apple manifest, and independent heading scans confirm 13 annual and 10 interim notes. The existing builder hard-codes selected statement/debt amounts, while interim Note 9 retains a generic unresolved disposition. P01’s accepted source register is in its run directory. Reuse the prior planning log’s verified findings and implement a new versioned module without rewriting preserved evidence. This plan addresses MC01, MC03, MC05, MC16 and MC28 without closing the wider gaps.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    \"1. Establish the input and write boundaries. Read the accepted P01 register, Apple originals, extracted text, manifest and retained SEC submissions index. Recheck hashes and bind each original to its extraction and document identity. Create scripts/apple_case_v1.py and tests/test_accounting_p02.py. Write only case.json and result.md under data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02. Any newly acquired sources go into a new docs/design/cases/apple/p02-v1/ directory. Preserve existing builders, manifests, snapshots, benchmark files and controller files.\",\n    \"2. Implement reusable source-anchor and extraction functions. Annual anchors must include original/extraction hashes, PDF page, printed page where identifiable, exact text offsets and quotation; retain table headers and selected column locations. Interim extraction must resolve inline-XBRL fact, context and unit IDs from the retained HTML, including entity, instant/duration, dimensions, currency, scale, sign, decimals and supported transformation. Validate extracted values against rendered labels/text. Reject missing, ambiguous or unsupported interpretations rather than guessing. Keep source readings, annotations and derived results separate.\",\n    \"3. Build the 23-note disposition layer from actual source spans. Independently discover note boundaries, reconcile them with the inventory and exclude following auditor/MD&A sections. Give every note explicit linked quantities or a specific unresolved meaning, affected model areas, qualifications and cross-reference targets. Replace the generic interim Contingencies treatment with an anchored management assertion whose uncertainty is preserved without inventing a probability or zero liability. Record annual/interim policy differences from their own passages. Report inventory, numerical coverage and semantic coverage separately.\",\n    \"4. Implement context validation and exact reconciliation using Fraction or Decimal, with no binary-float tolerance. Select facts by concept, reporting date/period, entity, perimeter, dimensions, measurement basis and unit. Check annual/comparative/interim balance-sheet identities; annual principal-to-carrying and current/noncurrent debt bridges; interim statement debt against rounded narrative debt; annual and interim product/segment revenue totals separately against statement revenue; annual PP&E gross-to-net; and annual/interim cash-flow opening-plus-movements-to-closing balances. Preserve each operand’s source and explain every permitted context transformation.\",\n    \"5. Implement rounding-aware comparisons. Retain displayed values and precision separately from inferred intervals. Encode 97,341 − 321 − 358 = 96,662 and 10,912 + 85,750 = 96,662 as displayed annual debt identities, and 10,848 + 83,956 = 94,804 as the interim identity. Verify 94,804 million is compatible with the displayed 94.8 billion under an explicitly recorded rounding model. Distinguish carrying amount, principal, fair value and derivative notional. For rounded aggregates, propagate operand intervals exactly; never conceal mismatches with a broad epsilon.\",\n    \"6. Preserve unidentified histories explicitly. Link the disclosed fixed-rate debt, swap discussion and annual 14,575 million interest-rate notional while leaving contract allocation, reset dates, hedge coverage, interim exposure, asset cohorts and contingent outcomes unresolved where unsupported. Retain the existing financing stress only as a labelled conditional illustration, if included; do not promote its assumed exposure or zero-tax treatment into extracted facts. Do not manufacture a debt roll-forward from cash movements when FX, noncash and measurement movements remain unidentified.\",\n    \"7. Investigate incorporation and publication obligations. Enumerate exact annual Part III and exhibit-index targets, distinguish material already inside the retained PDF from external documents, and preserve internal-reference closure separately. Use the retained SEC index to identify the 2025 proxy accession 0001308179-25-000008 and the annual/interim filing identities. Inspect legitimate SEC or issuer sources for the proxy and financing agreements relevant to this slice. Preserve acquired bytes, hashes, retrieval times and exact supporting spans. Give remaining obligations their target document/exhibit, version, missing terms, consequence and next legitimate retrieval route. Keep mirror availability distinct from filing availability; a selected-table match does not establish whole-PDF publication equivalence.\",\n    \"8. Generate deterministic case.json containing source bindings, typed observations, all note dispositions, mappings, bridges, external obligations, availability records and unidentified-history records. Provide build and read-only --check CLI modes. result.md must record the pre-run evidence/default audit, actual commands, deterministic check results, changed-file hashes, environment, elapsed time, input/output paths, decision table and separate implementation/accounting/forecast/human-acceptance assessments. Use the reviewed phase packet as plan provenance; report unavailable Git provenance honestly.\"\n  ],\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    \"The case scope is Apple’s fiscal 2024 annual report and fiscal 2025 first-quarter report, retaining their disclosed comparatives. Apple’s fiscal calendar must come from the filings; calendar-year or generic 90-day substitutions are not permitted.\",\n    \"The existing manifest is an inventory and regression reference, not the numerical oracle. The accepted P01 register supplies provenance; the retained source passages supply the actual values.\",\n    \"The current core_semantics.py validator explicitly supports a frozen synthetic source. P02 therefore adds a separate bounded case module rather than claiming the existing validator accepts real filings.\",\n    \"Use standard-library arithmetic/parsing or already-installed dependencies. PDF text extraction uses the existing pdftotext capability. Missing capabilities receive one explicit residual and no installation, approval request or bypass.\",\n    \"Where the source establishes presentation precision but not tie-breaking, nearest-rounding intervals are a documented interpretation with conservative endpoints, not a proved issuer rule. Unsupported precision remains unresolved.\",\n    \"No scientific experiment, tuning comparison or forecasting run is required. Verification concerns deterministic extraction and arithmetic, so statistical superiority and a baseline performance ladder are inapplicable.\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": [\n    \"Skeptical audit: the plan replaces authored totals as truth with source-bound readings; guards against scale, sign, measurement and cash-perimeter mismatches; separates filing, retrieval and mirror availability; and uses deterministic rejection tests rather than semantic-coverage counts as promotion evidence. It avoids GPU/environment dependencies and contains no stochastic ranking.\",\n    \"Pre-run evidence contract: pass requires all 23 anchored note dispositions, successful supported bridges and expected adversarial rejections. Missing mandatory inputs, hash failures, ambiguous required extraction, unsupported context or failed arithmetic veto acceptance and trigger repair. External-access failure blocks only the unsupported incorporation/version claim; it must not erase independent completed work.\",\n    \"Run python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_accounting_p02.py -v. Tests must consume the real retained annual text/PDF and interim HTML, verify selected annual rows through independent pdftotext output, and use independently stated arithmetic expectations rather than importing expected results from the builder.\",\n    \"Test missing/duplicate notes, incorrect note boundaries, altered quotations and source hashes, broken fact/context/unit IDs, wrong scale/sign/currency/entity/perimeter/date, dimensional duplicates and conflicting repeated readings. Mutating supplied case metadata while leaving source bytes unchanged must fail revalidation.\",\n    \"Check the annual cash-flow opening balance of 30,737 against its own source perimeter; substituting balance-sheet cash of 29,965 must fail. Check product and geography partitions separately; combining both totals must fail. Reject substitution of fair value or derivative notional for debt carrying value.\",\n    \"Test compatible and incompatible rounded debt values, exact interval endpoints, unknown availability, later proxy evidence at earlier cutoffs and separately retained conflicting versions. No unknown publication timestamp may become a fabricated point timestamp.\",\n    \"Run python3 -B scripts/apple_case_v1.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02, then python3 -B scripts/apple_case_v1.py --check --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02. Require deterministic substantive output, valid source links and a report that preserves unresolved obligations.\",\n    \"Compare pre/post hashes of touched inputs and protected files; record every newly created source/code/test file. Run no controller, acquisition sweep, GPU diagnostic, background process or model worker.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"AGENTS.md\",\